   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch8/q3",
   "question": "<p>A scientist is studying the effect of introducing a population of white-clawed crayfish into a population of signal crayfish.<br>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years, the number of white-clawed crayfish, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w\"></span>, and the number of signal crayfish, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\"></span>, are modelled by the differential equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm dw}{\\mathrm dt}&amp;=\\frac52(w-s)\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm ds}{\\mathrm dt}&amp;=\\frac25w-90\\mathrm e^{-t}\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2\\frac{\\mathrm d^2w}{\\mathrm dt^2}-5\\frac{\\mathrm dw}{\\mathrm dt}+2w=450\\mathrm e^{-t}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Find a general solution for the number of white-clawed crayfish at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Find a general solution for the number of signal crayfish at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The model predicts that, at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> years, the population of white-clawed crayfish will have died out.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w=65\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s=85\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, giving your answer to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li><li>Suggest a limitation of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
    "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch8/q03-ms-p14-1.png\" width=\"880\" height=\"880\" alt=\"PMT mark scheme for Core Pure 2 Ch.8 Modelling with Differential Equations Q3; source page 14, segment 1 of 4. Includes the working, marks, alternative methods and notes in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
