   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch8/q4",
   "question": "<p>At the start of the year 2000, a survey began of the number of foxes and rabbits on an island.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years after the survey began, the number of foxes, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f\"></span>, and the number of rabbits, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span>, on the island are modelled by the differential equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm df}{\\mathrm dt}&amp;=0.2f+0.1r\\\\\\frac{\\mathrm dr}{\\mathrm dt}&amp;=-0.2f+0.4r\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\mathrm d^2f}{\\mathrm dt^2}-0.6\\dfrac{\\mathrm df}{\\mathrm dt}+0.1f=0\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Find a general solution for the number of foxes on the island at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence find a general solution for the number of rabbits on the island at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> years. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>At the start of the year 2000 there were 6 foxes and 20 rabbits on the island.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"4\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>According to this model, in which year are the rabbits predicted to die out?</li><li>According to this model, how many foxes will be on the island when the rabbits die out?</li><li>Use your answers to parts (i) and (ii) to comment on the model.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(7)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
