   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch8/q8",
   "question": "<p>A company plans to build a new fairground ride. The ride will consist of a capsule that will hold the passengers and the capsule will be attached to a tall tower. The capsule is to be released from rest from a point half way up the tower and then made to oscillate in a vertical line.<br>The vertical displacement, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> metres, of the top of the capsule below its initial position at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds is modelled by the differential equation,</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"m\\frac{\\mathrm d^2x}{\\mathrm dt^2}+4\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}+x=200\\cos t,\\quad t\\geqslant0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is the mass of the capsule including its passengers, in thousands of kilograms.</p><p>The maximum permissible weight for the capsule, including its passengers, is 30 000N.</p><p>Taking the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"g\"></span> to be 10 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm{ms^{-2}}\"></span> and assuming the capsule is at its maximum permissible weight,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>explain why the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> is 3</li><li><p>show that a particular solution to the differential equation is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=40\\sin t-20\\cos t\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li><li>hence find the general solution of the differential equation.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></li><li>Using the model, find, to the nearest metre, the vertical distance of the top of the capsule from its initial position, 9 seconds after it is released. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
   "steps": [
    "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/pmt/pure-core-2-ch8/q08-ms-p24-1.png\" width=\"870\" height=\"824\" alt=\"PMT mark scheme for Core Pure 2 Ch.8 Modelling with Differential Equations Q8; source page 24, segment 1 of 3. Includes the working, marks, alternative methods and notes in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
